/*!
@defgroup etmr_mc_driver eTMR Timer/Counter Driver (eTMR_MC)
@ingroup etmr
@details
@brief Timer/Counter mode driver for the eTMR peripheral.

## Overview

The MC (Module Counter) sub-module provides basic timer/counter
functionality. It supports up-counting and center-aligned modes,
with configurable period and initial counter values.

## Usage Pattern

@code{.c}
#define ETMR_INST (0U)

etmr_state_t state;
etmr_user_config_t config;
etmr_timer_param_t timerParam;

/* Step 1: Initialize eTMR common driver */
eTMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&config);
eTMR_DRV_Init(ETMR_INST, &config, &state);

/* Step 2: Configure timer parameters */
timerParam.mode        = eTMR_MODE_UP_TIMER;
timerParam.initialValue = 0U;
timerParam.finalValue   = 0x8000U;
eTMR_DRV_InitCounter(ETMR_INST, &timerParam);

/* Step 3: Start counting */
eTMR_DRV_CounterStart(ETMR_INST);

/* ... application logic ... */

/* Step 4: Stop and de-initialize */
eTMR_DRV_CounterStop(ETMR_INST);
eTMR_DRV_Deinit(ETMR_INST);
@endcode

## API Quick Reference

| Function | Description |
|---|---|
| eTMR_DRV_InitCounter() | Configure counter mode, initial and final values. |
| eTMR_DRV_CounterStart() | Start the free-running counter. |
| eTMR_DRV_CounterStop() | Stop the counter. |
| eTMR_DRV_CounterRead() | Read the current counter value. |

*/
